  "query_preview": "..\nShower coverage has gradually increased with the approach of Invest\n92W and is expected to become numerous tonight through tomorrow, with\nwet conditions lasting longer for Guam and Rota. Isolated \nthunderstorms were observed today and are expected to continue\nthrough Friday night. These thunderstorms and heavier showers could\nhave gusty winds through Friday. As discussed in the Tropical \nSystems section below, Invest 92W remains unlikely to pass through \nthe Marianas as a tropical storm. However, the Marianas should still \nexpect increasing showers, isolated thunderstorms, building seas and \nsurf, and stronger winds. Afterwards, a ridge of high pressure will \nfill in once 92W passes, bringing drier conditions to the Marianas. \nLight winds could allow for island effect showers and thunderstorms \nin the afternoon periods Sunday and Monday.",
